              "title": "There must be no shosts.equiv files on the RHEL 8 operating system.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>The shosts.equiv files are used to configure host-based authentication for the system via SSH. Host-based authentication is not sufficient for preventing unauthorized access to the system.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230283",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000883-GPOS-00023",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230283r1130283_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230283r1130283_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-010460",
          "rule_title": "There must be no shosts.equiv files on the RHEL 8 operating system.",
          "fix_text": "Remove any found \"shosts.equiv\" files from the system.\n\n$ sudo rm /etc/ssh/shosts.equiv",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify there are no \"shosts.equiv\" files on RHEL 8 with the following command:\n\n$ sudo find / -name shosts.equiv\n\nIf a \"shosts.equiv\" file is found, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "The shosts.equiv files are used to configure host-based authentication for the system via SSH. Host-based authentication is not sufficient for preventing unauthorized access to the system.",
