            {
              "id": "V-230286",
              "title": "The RHEL 8 SSH daemon must perform strict mode checking of home directory configuration files.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>If other users have access to modify user-specific SSH configuration files, they may be able to log on to the system as another user.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230286",
          "severity": "high",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000886-GPOS-00024",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230286r1130286_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230286r1130286_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-010500",
          "rule_title": "The RHEL 8 SSH daemon must perform strict mode checking of home directory configuration files.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the SSH daemon to perform strict mode checking of home directory configuration files.\n\nUncomment the \"StrictModes\" keyword in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config\" and set the value to \"yes\":\n\nStrictModes yes\n\nThe SSH service must be restarted for changes to take effect.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the SSH daemon performs strict mode checking of home directory configuration files with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grep -i strictmodes /etc/ssh/sshd_config\nStrictModes yes\n\nIf \"StrictModes\" is set to \"no\", is missing, or the returned line is commented out, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "If other users have access to modify user-specific SSH configuration files, they may be able to log on to the system as another user.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": false,
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
