              "title": "The rsyslog service must be running in RHEL 8.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Configuring RHEL 8 to implement organization-wide security implementation guides and security checklists ensures compliance with federal standards.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230301",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000901-GPOS-00026",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230301r1130301_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230301r1130301_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-010561",
          "rule_title": "The rsyslog service must be running in RHEL 8.",
          "fix_text": "Start the \"rsyslog\" service and enable it to start at boot with the following commands:\n\n$ sudo systemctl enable --now rsyslog",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify that \"rsyslog\" is being used to monitor auditing on the system.\n\nCheck that the \"rsyslog\" service is enabled and active with the following commands:\n\n$ sudo systemctl is-enabled rsyslog\nenabled\n\n$ sudo systemctl is-active rsyslog\nactive\n\nIf the service is not enabled and active, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Configuring RHEL 8 to implement organization-wide security implementation guides and security checklists ensures compliance with federal standards.",
