              "id": "V-230386",
              "title": "RHEL 8 audit records must be off-loaded onto a different system or storage media from the system being audited.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Information stored in one location is vulnerable to accidental or incidental deletion or alteration.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230386",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000986-GPOS-00038",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230386r1130386_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230386r1130386_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-030000",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 audit records must be off-loaded onto a different system or storage media from the system being audited.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the audit system to off-load audit records onto a different system or media from the system being audited.\n\nSet the remote server option in \"/etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf\" with the IP address of the log aggregation server.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the audit system off-loads audit records onto a different system or media from the system being audited with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grep -i remote_server /etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf\nremote_server = 10.0.21.1\n\nIf a remote server is not configured, or the line is commented out, ask the System Administrator to indicate how the audit logs are off-loaded to a different system or media.\n\nIf there is no evidence that the audit logs are being off-loaded to another system or media, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Information stored in one location is vulnerable to accidental or incidental deletion or alteration.",
