              "id": "V-230387",
              "title": "RHEL 8 audit system must take appropriate action when the audit storage volume is full.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>It is critical that when RHEL 8 is at risk of failing to process audit logs as required, it takes action to mitigate the failure.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230387",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000987-GPOS-00039",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230387r1130387_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230387r1130387_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-030010",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 audit system must take appropriate action when the audit storage volume is full.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the audit system to take an appropriate action when the audit storage volume is full.\n\nAdd or modify the following line in \"/etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf\":\n\ndisk_full_action = single",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify RHEL 8 takes the appropriate action when the audit storage volume is full with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grep disk_full_action /etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf\ndisk_full_action = single\n\nIf the value of the \"disk_full_action\" option is not \"syslog\", \"single\", or \"halt\", or the line is commented out, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "It is critical that when RHEL 8 is at risk of failing to process audit logs as required, it takes action to mitigate the failure.",
