          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-230396",
              "title": "RHEL 8 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Without the capability to generate audit records, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230396",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000996-GPOS-00041",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230396r1130396_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230396r1130396_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-030063",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon.",
          "fix_text": "Configure RHEL 8 to allocate sufficient audit_backlog_limit to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=audit_backlog_limit=8192\n\nAdd the argument to the default grub config so it persists across kernel updates:\n\nEdit \"/etc/default/grub\" and add \"audit_backlog_limit=8192\" to the GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX line.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify RHEL 8 allocates a sufficient audit_backlog_limit with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grub2-editenv list | grep audit\nkernelopts=root=/dev/mapper/rhel-root ro crashkernel=auto resume=/dev/mapper/rhel-swap rd.lvm.lv=rhel/root rd.lvm.lv=rhel/swap rhgb quiet fips=1 audit=1 audit_backlog_limit=8192\n\nIf the \"audit_backlog_limit\" entry does not equal or exceed \"8192\", is missing, or the line is commented out, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Without the capability to generate audit records, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": false,
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "legacy_ids": [
            "SV-87396r792904_rule",
            "V-87396"
          ],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000996"
          ],
          "status": "not_a_finding",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "",
          "finding_details": "Scanned by synthetic fixture generator. RHEL-08-030063 matched the required value."
