            {
              "id": "V-230423",
              "title": "Successful/unsuccessful modifications to the faillock log file in RHEL 8 must generate an audit record.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Without generating audit records that are specific to the security and mission needs of the organization, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230423",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000123-GPOS-00042",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230423r1130423_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230423r1130423_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-030170",
          "rule_title": "Successful/unsuccessful modifications to the faillock log file in RHEL 8 must generate an audit record.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the audit system to generate an audit event for any modification to the \"/etc/sudoers\" file.\n\nAdd or update the following rule in \"/etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules\":\n\n-w /etc/sudoers -p wa -k identity\n\nThe audit daemon must be restarted for the changes to take effect:\n\n$ sudo augenrules --load",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify RHEL 8 generates an audit record for all modifications to the \"/etc/sudoers\" file with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grep /etc/sudoers /etc/audit/audit.rules\n-w /etc/sudoers -p wa -k identity\n\nIf the command does not return a line, or the line is commented out, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Without generating audit records that are specific to the security and mission needs of the organization, it would be difficult to establish, correlate, and investigate the events relating to an incident.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": false,
          "security_override_guidance": "",
