            {
              "id": "V-230486",
              "title": "RHEL 8 audit tools must have a mode of 0755 or less permissive.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Protecting audit information also includes identifying and protecting the tools used to view and manipulate log data.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230486",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000186-GPOS-00045",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230486r1130486_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230486r1130486_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-030620",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 audit tools must have a mode of 0755 or less permissive.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the audit tools to have a mode of \"0755\" or less permissive with the following command:\n\n$ sudo chmod 0755 /sbin/auditctl /sbin/aureport /sbin/ausearch /sbin/autrace /sbin/auditd /sbin/rsyslogd /sbin/augenrules",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the audit tools have a mode of \"0755\" or less permissive with the following command:\n\n$ sudo stat -c \"%a %n\" /sbin/auditctl /sbin/aureport /sbin/ausearch /sbin/autrace /sbin/auditd /sbin/rsyslogd /sbin/augenrules\n755 /sbin/auditctl\n\nIf any of the audit tools have a mode more permissive than \"0755\", this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Protecting audit information also includes identifying and protecting the tools used to view and manipulate log data.",
