              "id": "V-230507",
              "title": "RHEL 8 must be configured to disable USB mass storage.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>USB mass storage permits easy introduction of unknown devices, thereby facilitating malicious activity.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230507",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000207-GPOS-00050",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230507r1130507_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230507r1130507_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-040060",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 must be configured to disable USB mass storage.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the operating system to disable the ability to use the USB Storage kernel module.\n\nAdd or update the following lines in the file \"/etc/modprobe.d/blacklist.conf\":\n\ninstall usb-storage /bin/false\nblacklist usb-storage",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify the operating system disables the ability to load the USB Storage kernel module with the following command:\n\n$ sudo grep -ri usb-storage /etc/modprobe.d/ | grep -i \"/bin/false\"\ninstall usb-storage /bin/false\n\nIf the command does not return any output, or the line is commented out, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "USB mass storage permits easy introduction of unknown devices, thereby facilitating malicious activity.",
