              "id": "V-230514",
              "title": "RHEL 8 wireless network adapters must be disabled.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Without protection of communications with wireless peripherals, confidentiality and integrity may be compromised.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230514",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000214-GPOS-00053",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230514r1130514_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230514r1130514_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-040110",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 wireless network adapters must be disabled.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the system to disable all wireless network interfaces with the following command:\n\n$ sudo nmcli radio all off",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify there are no wireless interfaces configured on the system with the following command:\n\nNote: This requirement is Not Applicable for systems that do not have physical wireless network radios.\n\n$ sudo nmcli device status\n\nIf a wireless interface is configured and its use on the system is not documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO) as an operational requirement, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Without protection of communications with wireless peripherals, confidentiality and integrity may be compromised.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
