              "title": "The x86 Ctrl-Alt-Delete key sequence must be disabled on RHEL 8.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>A locally logged-on user who presses Ctrl-Alt-Delete, when at the console, can reboot the system.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230539",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000239-GPOS-00056",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230539r1130539_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230539r1130539_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-040170",
          "rule_title": "The x86 Ctrl-Alt-Delete key sequence must be disabled on RHEL 8.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the system to disable the Ctrl-Alt-Delete sequence for the command line with the following commands:\n\n$ sudo systemctl disable --now ctrl-alt-del.target\n$ sudo systemctl mask --now ctrl-alt-del.target",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify RHEL 8 is not configured to reboot the system when Ctrl-Alt-Delete is pressed with the following command:\n\n$ sudo systemctl status ctrl-alt-del.target\nctrl-alt-del.target\n   Loaded: masked (Reason: Unit ctrl-alt-del.target is masked.)\n   Active: inactive (dead)\n\nIf the ctrl-alt-del.target is not masked, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "A locally logged-on user who presses Ctrl-Alt-Delete, when at the console, can reboot the system.",
