              "title": "The RHEL 8 operating system must implement DoD-approved encryption in the OpenSSL package.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Without cryptographic integrity protections, information can be altered by unauthorized users without detection.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230236",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000836-GPOS-00060",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230236r1130236_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230236r1130236_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-010150",
          "rule_title": "The RHEL 8 operating system must implement DoD-approved encryption in the OpenSSL package.",
          "fix_text": "The ISSO will document and obtain written approval for any deviation from the DoD-approved cryptographic policy, or remove the deviation.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify that system-wide crypto policies are in effect and the site has documented its deviations, if any.\n\nThe Information System Security Officer (ISSO) will verify that any deviation from the DoD-approved cryptographic policy is documented, justified, and approved in writing.\n\nIf deviations exist and are not documented and approved, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "Without cryptographic integrity protections, information can be altered by unauthorized users without detection.",
