              "id": "V-230392",
              "title": "RHEL 8 must take appropriate action when an audit processing failure occurs and notify designated personnel.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>It is critical for the appropriate personnel to be aware if a system is at risk of failing to process audit logs as required.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230392",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000992-GPOS-00066",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230392r1130392_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230392r1130392_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-030040",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 must take appropriate action when an audit processing failure occurs and notify designated personnel.",
          "fix_text": "Document the audit processing failure notification procedure, identify the designated personnel by role, and obtain ISSO approval.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify that designated personnel are notified when an audit processing failure occurs.\n\nAsk the System Administrator to identify the designated personnel and demonstrate how they are notified. Review the notification procedure with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nIf there is no documented notification procedure, or the designated personnel are not identified, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclass",
          "discussion": "It is critical for the appropriate personnel to be aware if a system is at risk of failing to process audit logs as required.",
