              "title": "RHEL 8 must have an approved contingency plan for restoring the system after a failure.",
              "description": "<GroupDescription>Without a contingency plan, restoration of the system after a failure is unlikely to meet the organization's recovery time objective.</GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-230498",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-OS-000198-GPOS-00067",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-230498r1130498_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-230498r1130498_rule",
          "rule_version": "RHEL-08-040004",
          "rule_title": "RHEL 8 must have an approved contingency plan for restoring the system after a failure.",
          "fix_text": "Develop a contingency plan for the system, test it annually, document the results, and obtain ISSO approval.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Verify an approved contingency plan exists for the system.\n\nThe Information System Security Officer (ISSO) will verify the plan is current, has been tested within the last year, and that the test results are documented.\n\nIf no current, tested contingency plan exists, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
